test.yaml:44:14: "npm publish" publishes to npm with the long-lived credential NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, although the job can request an OIDC token ("id-token: write"). prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:50:14: "cargo publish" publishes to crates.io with the long-lived credential CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN, although the job can request an OIDC token ("id-token: write"). prefer trusted publishing with rust-lang/crates-io-auth-action and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:64:14: "cargo publish" publishes to crates.io with the long-lived credential CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN, although the job can request an OIDC token ("id-token: write"). prefer trusted publishing with rust-lang/crates-io-auth-action and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
